1
00:00:04,671 --> 00:00:06,841
(Sheldon:)Oh, boy.

2
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:09,089
(Leonard:)What?

3
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:14,179
(Sheldon:)I can't comment without violating our
agreement that I not criticize your work.

4
00:00:14,347 --> 00:00:19,347
- Then what was "Oh, boy"?
- Great restraint on my part.

5
00:00:19,769 --> 00:00:21,939
(Leonard:)There's nothing wrong
with the science here.

6
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:26,695
(Sheldon:)Perhaps you mean a different thing
than I do when you say "science."

7
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:34,785
(Leonard(making a change):)Okay, how's that?

8
00:00:35,201 --> 00:00:37,581
(Sheldon:)You actually had it right
in the first place.

9
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:43,045
(Sheldon:)Once again, you've fallen
for one of my classic pranks.

10
00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:44,459
Buzzinga.

11
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:52,013
(Sheldon:)Well, now, here's a peculiar e-mail.

12
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:56,307
(Sheldon:)The president of the university wants me
to meet him at his office at 8 a.m.

13
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:59,513
(Howard:)- Why?
- Doesn't say. Must be an emergency.

14
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:02,354
Everyone at the university knows
I eat breakfast at 8...

15
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,810
...and move my bowels at 8:20.

16
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:09,022
(Leonard:)Yes, how did we live before Twitter?

17
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:13,240
(Leonard:)I guess you'll find out what it is
in the morning.

18
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:15,076
(Sheldon:)That's 14 hours away.

19
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:19,201
(Sheldon:)For the next 840 minutes, I'm effectively
one of Heisenberg's particles.

20
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:22,500
I know where I am or how fast I'm going,
but I can't know both.

21
00:01:22,665 --> 00:01:24,585
(Sheldon:)Yet how am I supposed to carry on...

22
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:27,671
(Sheldon:)...with this huge annoying thing
hovering over my head?

23
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:31,019
(Leonard:)Yeah, I know the feeling.

